### Design Rationale Summary:

| Task | Rule Type | Why |
|------|-----------|-----|
| mine allium | inventory_has(allium, 1) | Mined flower drops as item into inventory; player starts with 0 |
| mine hay_block | inventory_has(hay_block, 1) | Mined hay bale drops itself into inventory; player starts with 0 |
| sell Red Dye | inventory_has(emerald, 1) | Trading red dye to shepherd yields emerald; player starts with 0 |
| sell Pink Dye | inventory_has(emerald, 2) | Trading pink dye yields 2nd emerald; enforces sell_Red_Dye ordering |

### Ordering Enforcement:
- The emerald count naturally enforces the dependency `sell Red Dye → sell Pink Dye` (can't have 2 emeralds without completing both trades)
- The mining tasks have no inventory-based ordering enforcement, but the dependency graph handles sequencing at the evaluation level
- All rules use the simplest possible detection: items appearing in an initially-empty inventory slot
